#X text 149 147 “Ambient Music is intended to induce calm and space to think \; Ambient Music must be able to accommodate many levels of listening attention without enforce one in particular \; it must be as ignorable as interesting.” \; -Brian Eno September 1978 Liner notes from the initial American release of Brian Eno’s “Music for Airports/Ambient 1.”, f 100;
#X text 149 248 Analyze our gavourite ambient pieces;
#X text 149 297 Compositional characteristics of ambient music \; - Slow tempo (60 BPM of Accents) \; - Simple harmonic progressions (i-iv in C major) \; - Soft and non-abrasive sounds(LOP filtered sawtooth waves with slow attacks and release times). \; - Simple instrumentation(Bass & Melody) \; - Reverb is the best friend(utilize freeverb~), f 86;
